  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Electrical contractors and other wiring installation contractors (NAICS 238210) have seen smaller federal obligations in FY2026 to date compared with prior years. The federal government obligated $437M through FY2026 to date on NAICS 238210 work. The market recorded 1,945 awards with an average award size of $224K. Obligations fell 44.8% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows higher annual obligations from FY21 through FY25, including $792M in FY21, $853M in FY22, $945M in FY23, $824M in FY24, and $791M in FY25. The Department of Defense led buying in FY2026 to date with $115M in obligations, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $105M and the Department of State with $76.9M. XATOR LLC, SINTELA INC, and WSP USA SOLUTIONS INC are the largest contractors in FY2026 to date with $58.7M, $36.3M, and $22.8M respectively. These figures cover fiscal year to date obligations and reflect partial current-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal demand for NAICS 238210 changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 44.8% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows a peak of $945M in FY23 and lower totals thereafter, including $791M in FY25 and $437M in FY26 to date. The market recorded 1,945 awards in FY2026 to date with an average award size of $224K."
      },
